## Understanding Teams

In StoryBook, all projects and assets belong to a **Team** (also called a Studio). This allows you to collaborate with
others without sharing your personal login credentials.

### Creating a Team

1. Click the **Team Selector** in the sidebar (top-left).
2. Click **Create Team**.
3. Enter a name for your Studio (e.g., "DreamWorks Beta").
4. Click **Create**.

You can switch between teams using the same selector.

## Member Roles

When inviting members to your team, you can assign them specific roles:

| Role | Permissions |
| :--- | :--- |
| **Owner** | Full access. Can manage billing, delete the team, and manage all members. |
| **Admin** | Can manage projects, assets, and invite/remove members. Cannot manage billing or delete the team. |
| **Member** | Can view and edit projects and assets. Cannot manage team settings or invite others. |

## Managing Members

### Inviting Members

1. Go to **Settings → Members**.
2. Click **Invite Member**.
3. Enter their email address and select a Role.
4. Click **Send Invitation**.

The user will receive an email to join your team. If they don't have an account, they will be prompted to create one.

### Removing Members

1. Go to **Settings → Members**.
2. Find the user in the list.
3. Click the **Context Menu (...)** and select **Remove**.